{"text": "To: \u2018Memorandum to the File\n\nFROM: Diana Grub Frieser\nCity Attorney\nDATE: November 22, 2011\n\nSUBJECT: \u2014_Confict of Interest Inquiry from Susan Haynie\n\nPart |; Basic Fact.\n\n\u2018On Thursday, November 17, 2011, Susan Haynie contacted me regarding a potential conflict of interest\n\u2018She advised me of the following facts relating to the upcoming appeal of a site plan for 831 E. Palmetto\nark Road (a property owned by James Batmasian, individually). She and her husband own a property\nmanagement company that manages numerous real property sites, but, in particular, has a property\n\u2018management contract with a master condominium association for residential property in Broward County.\n\u2018The master association is named Tivoli Park Master Association, Inc. (\"Master Association\u2019) and is\n\u2018comprised of three residential condominium associations. Ms. Haynie advised me that one of the three\n\u2018condominium associations is a 200+ residential units complex that is owned wholly by the Batmasians\n\u2018and the units are made available for ental. The contract for property management services is an annual\ncontract and was entered into prior to the Palm Beach County ethics ordinance taking effect. The inquiry\nis whether the contractual relationship between Ms. Haynie\u2019s company and the Master Association\ncreates a voting conflict for Ms. Haynie in connection with the upcoming appeal to be heard by the City\nCouncil regarding 831 E, Palmetto Park Road\n\nPart Il: Additional Information:\n\nWe obtained supplemental information from Ms. Haynie that demonstrates that the Master Association is\nactually comprised of six separate condominium associations or apartment complexes, with an aggregate\ncof approximately 1600 units, and that all but approximately 200 of these units are owned or controlled\neither by the Batmasians andor business entities in which they have a controling interest. Additionally,\ntwo of the three listed officers of the Master Association are connected to Investments Ltd., which is a\nbusiness entity owned or controlled by the Batmasians,\n\nPart il: Analysis and Conclusion:\na. Florida Ethics Code of Ethics",
